==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Gentleman Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Gentleman Bros.''' when obtained from [[Evil Cat Awakes!]] (may be dropped on the first stage but guaranteed on the second stage) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
High cost and weak stats prevent him from being viable prior to true form unless you don't have any good counters to [[Bore]] (which most likely won't happen since there are a lot of [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|Anti Red]] [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|CC]]) . However, if you have [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Lesser Demon Cat]], you could find use in their combo [[Speak of the Devil (Combo)|Speak Of The Devil]] in [[:Category:Li'l Stages|Li'l Stages]] and {{4c}} [[Stories of Legend#Crown Difficulty|Stories of Legend]] stages.

==='''True Form'''===
Gentleman Bros is significantly better in terms of stacking them to permafreeze Red enemies. However, his bad stats, horrible range, low freeze chance, and single target prevent him from being useful, as he is still outclassed by better anti-red Cats, such as [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Apple Cat]], and [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Witch Cat]].

Gentleman Bros. ''can'' be used against [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]] with Barriers due to its [[Barrier Breaker]] ability if no better alternatives are available in [[Cats of the Cosmos]] [[Restriction Stage]]s, though they are again hindered by having low stats and poor range that prevent them from reaching some in the first place.

