==Trivia==
*Gentleman Bros. were among the units that were given [[Barrier Breaker]] in [[Version 6.5 Update|Version 6.5]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Evil Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Evil Cat
Hides his weakness by wearing the
the mask of the demon.
Might stop Red enemies.</pre>
<pre>Gentleman Cat
A very well clothed cat. Until…
Just call the police.
Might stop Red enemies.</pre>
<pre>Gentleman Bros.
A gentleman's agreement makes life easier
for everyone. But whoever's on bottom has
it worse. Might stop Red and break Barriers!</pre>
**Evil Cat's original English description contained an error, with two '''the'''s in a row. "Hides his weakness by wearing '''the the''' mask of the demon."
*The unusual Japanese name for Evil Cat references the title of Natsume Sōseki's famous novel ''[[wikipedia:I Am a Cat|I Am a Cat]]''. The personal pronoun employed in the title is deemed pompous and almost exclusively used in 'cat speech' in the modern era.
*Evil Cat's appearance and Japanese description reference the ''[[wikipedia:Setsubun#Traditions|mamemaki]]'' (豆撒き, ''bean scattering'') tradition of [[wikipedia:Setsubun|Setsubun]] where roasted soybeans are thrown at a family member wearing an oni mask. They could also be a reference to the [[wikipedia:Namahage|Namahage]], men dressed as oni and brandishing knives.
*The first form's attack animation is similar to [[Zombie Cat (Special Cat)|Zombie Cat]]'s, albeit with the arms being swung to the ground and the head shaking.

